  "reason": "Patient endorses a longstanding, childhood-onset pattern of inattentive symptoms (losing track of reading material and meeting content, leaving tasks unfinished at the final step, being told by others he 'leaves things unfinished') combined with hyperactive-impulsive symptoms (inability to remain seated in meetings, subjective restlessness, interrupting/blurting out answers before others finish). Childhood history supports onset prior to age 12 (teacher reports of being 'bright but rushed,' talking out of turn, disorganized desk, forgotten homework). Both inattentive and hyperactive-impulsive symptom clusters are clearly present, meeting criteria for combined presentation (F90.2) rather than a single subtype. Cross-setting impairment was probed extensively; while work impairment is robust and clearly documented, home/social impairment was only partially corroborated (partner comment about 'leaving things unfinished,' some vague acknowledgment of distractibility at home) without the patient generating clean independent examples outside work, which is a limitation but does not negate the diagnosis given the strength and pervasiveness of the core symptom pattern and clear childhood-onset trajectory.",
  "diagnostic_checklist": {
    "symptom_groups": [
      {
        "group": "inattention",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "Difficulty sustaining attention during long meetings, losing track of content while appearing to listen",
          "Difficulty sustaining attention while reading client briefs, having to reread passages",
          "Failure to complete the final step of tasks (e.g., not sending final proposal, not logging CRM follow-up) despite believing task was finished",
          "History of childhood inattentiveness: rushing through schoolwork, forgetting homework, disorganized desk with unfinished worksheets",
          "Being told by a partner that he 'leaves things unfinished'",
          "Missing key parts of conversations/feedback despite appearing attentive, requiring repetition"
        ],
        "count": 6
      },
      {
        "group": "hyperactivity_impulsivity",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "Inability to remain seated during long meetings, needing to get up and pace or find reasons to move (e.g., refilling water, walking to printer)",
          "Subjective sense of restlessness occurring independent of anxious or worried thoughts",
          "Interrupting others or blurting out answers before they finish speaking, particularly with clients/coworkers",
          "History of talking out of turn in childhood"
        ],
        "count": 4
      }
